From: SkillBuddy Agent <agent@skillbuddy.local>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 11:42:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Booking Confirmation, Payment System, Job Tracking state
 machine, and Call screen (Sections 3-5)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Section 3 — Booking Confirmation & Assignment:
- Accept Bid now shows a real confirmation summary (provider, price,
  date/time, job title) before routing into payment instead of
  directly assigning.
- New Booking Summary screen after successful payment: success state,
  assigned provider card with chat/call access, job details.

Section 4 — Payment System UI:
- lib/payment.ts: calculateOrderBreakdown() and calculatePayoutBreakdown()
  as real functions (not hardcoded numbers) — verified against the
  spec's worked example (€30 bid -> €24.19 before VAT, €5.81 VAT,
  matches exactly).
- Payment screen: method selection (Card/Apple Pay/Google Pay/Bank
  Transfer/Credit Points), real Pay Later / Instalments eligibility
  logic driven by the mock user's completed-task count and bill
  amount (not just always-shown options), Credit Points toggle
  (1 pt = €0.10) that recalculates the total live, and a real
  10-minute countdown that reopens the job for bidding if it expires
  without payment completing.

Section 5 — Job Tracking, Updating & Completion:
- Expanded JobStatus to the full spec'd state machine (draft, bidding,
  short_listed, task_assigned, pending_payment, arrived, in_progress,
  revision_requested, completed, approved, closed, cancelled, expired,
  disputed, paused) and updated all existing 'assigned' references
  consistently to 'task_assigned'.
- New Job Tracking screen: visual status stepper, provider-side
  'I've Arrived' -> 'Start Job' -> 'Mark as Done' flow (irreversible
  confirmation), propose/respond-to Revision (extra hours + new price,
  pending/approved/denied states for both sides), Cancel Job flow with
  distinct provider-cancels (credibility/rating penalty, mock 28-day
  suspension if rating drops below 4.0) vs client-cancels (€5
  cancellation fee) consequences, and the provider payout breakdown
  inline.
- New Review screen: Approve (rating + feedback, finalizes payment),
  Deny (required written feedback, capped at 2 denials — UI disables
  further denial and shows why), Dispute (reason list + required
  description, creates a mock support ticket, flags job Disputed).
- Jobs tab now routes assigned/in-progress jobs to the tracking screen
  instead of the bidding dashboard, which is bidding-phase-only.

Chat & Call:
- Added a phone icon to the Chat Thread header, wired to a new
  simulated Active Call screen (mute, speaker/earpiece toggle, end
  call, duration timer capped at 5 minutes with a 'call ending soon'
  warning near the limit).

Full workspace typecheck: zero errors.

Not yet covered in this pass (follow-up): chat delivery/read receipts,
image/voice message size-limit UI copy, the 90-day peer-chat vs
permanent support-chat lifecycle distinction, payment retry-on-failure
UI, and the remaining edge-case empty states from Section 5.
